// E2E families x constructs matrix for ADR 0122 (Unify `ThreadedIr`
// Storage-Family Threading) — BT-3519, the epic's close-out issue.
//
// Every one of BT-3509 through BT-3518 landed a Rust-level (unit/BUnit)
// migration; none of them exercised the REPL's own `:load`/eval path, which
// is a materially different code path (Workspace class registration, live
// gen_server class/actor processes, REPL response formatting) than a
// `cargo test -p beamtalk-codegen` or `just test-bunit` run. This file
// proves the three storage families ADR 0122 unified — Actor `state:`,
// class-method `classState:`, and value-type `TestCase` field — thread
// correctly through each construct, end-to-end, via `:load` + a live method
// call, and that the shapes still rejected at compile time (ADR 0122's own
// decision, not a bug) fail with the expected diagnostic.
//
// Fixtures (one class per file so a REJECTED method never keeps a whole
// fixture from loading):
//   storage_family_actor.bt                    — Actor `state:`, all ACCEPT
//   storage_family_class_method.bt              — class `classState:`, all ACCEPT
//   storage_family_class_method_ensure_direct_write.bt — classState direct write in ensure:
//   storage_family_class_method_foldl_direct_write.bt  — classState direct write in do:
//   storage_family_value_type.bt                — TestCase field, ACCEPT cells
//   storage_family_value_type_foldl_reject.bt      — TestCase field REJECT (do:)
//   storage_family_value_type_match_reject.bt      — TestCase field REJECT (match:)
//
// Ground-truth values mirror the already-verified BUnit corpus fragments
// (stdlib/test/fixtures/mutation_corpus_actor.bt,
// stdlib/test/fixtures/mutation_corpus_class_method.bt,
// stdlib/test/value_type_mutation_matrix_test.bt's `frag*` methods) rather
// than being independently derived here.

// ===========================================================================
// FAMILY 1: Actor `state:` — every construct ACCEPTS (ADR 0122: `State`
// threads unconditionally, never a function of body shape).
// ===========================================================================

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_actor.bt
// => Loaded: StorageFamilyActor

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) toDo
// => 15

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) whileTrue
// => 5

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) ifTrueIfFalse: true
// => 1

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) ifTrueIfFalse: false
// => 100

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) collectSum
// => 6

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) onDo
// => 3

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) ensure
// => 1

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) matchArm: 1
// => 1

(StorageFamilyActor spawn) matchArm: 2
// => 0

// ===========================================================================
// FAMILY 2: class-method `classState:` — `to:do:`/`whileTrue:`/
// `ifTrue:ifFalse:`, `do:`/`collect:` and `on:do:`/`ensure:` accept a bare
// direct class-var write (ADR 0122 / BT-3506; ADR 0130 removed the
// compile-time rejections that used to stop the last two).
// ===========================================================================

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_class_method.bt
// => Loaded: StorageFamilyClassMethod

StorageFamilyClassMethod toDo
// => 15

StorageFamilyClassMethod whileTrue
// => 5

StorageFamilyClassMethod ifTrueIfFalse: true
// => 1

StorageFamilyClassMethod ifTrueIfFalse: false
// => 100

StorageFamilyClassMethod doViaSelfSend
// => 3

StorageFamilyClassMethod onDoViaSelfSend
// => 1

// BT-3506's own headline repro (ADR 0122 "A sixth gap"), verbatim, now
// proven through the REPL's own load/eval path: before the fix this
// compiled via the closure path and silently discarded the self-send's
// mutation, returning 0.
StorageFamilyClassMethod ensureViaSelfSendOnly
// => 1

StorageFamilyClassMethod matchArm: 1
// => 1

StorageFamilyClassMethod matchArm: 2
// => 0

// ── A bare direct class-var write nested inside `ensure:` compiles (ADR 0130:
// the write is an in-place `put`; before it was the compile-time rejection
// ClassVarAssignmentInThreadedBody) and is kept.
:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_class_method_ensure_direct_write.bt
// => Loaded: StorageFamilyClassMethodEnsureDirectWrite

StorageFamilyClassMethodEnsureDirectWrite ensureDirectWrite
// => 1

// ── A bare direct class-var write inside a `do:` body compiles too (it used
// to fall through to the generic stored-closure-body rejection) and every
// iteration's write is kept.
:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_class_method_foldl_direct_write.bt
// => Loaded: StorageFamilyClassMethodFoldlDirectWrite

StorageFamilyClassMethodFoldlDirectWrite doDirectWrite
// => 6

// ===========================================================================
// FAMILY 3: value-type `TestCase` field — `to:do:`/`whileTrue:`/
// `ifTrue:ifFalse:` (BT-3484) and `on:do:`/`ensure:` (BT-3486) accept a bare
// top-level `self.field := ...` write; `do:`/`collect:` (BT-3487/BT-3488)
// and `match:` (BT-3489) are compile-time rejections.
// ===========================================================================

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_value_type.bt
// => Loaded: StorageFamilyValueType

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragToDo
// => 15

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragWhileTrue
// => 5

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragIfTrueIfFalse: true
// => 1

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragIfTrueIfFalse: false
// => 100

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragOnDo
// => 3

(StorageFamilyValueType new) fragEnsure
// => 1

// ── REJECT: a value-type field write inside a Foldl-shaped `do:` body has
// no matching accumulator slot to thread through — clean compile-time
// rejection (FieldAssignmentInUnsupportedBlock) rather than the erlc
// "unbound variable 'State'" crash it used to produce (BT-3487/BT-3488).
:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_value_type_foldl_reject.bt
// => ERROR: Cannot assign to field 'total' inside this block

_error kind
// => compile_error

// ── REJECT: a value-type field write as a `match:` arm body — `match:`'s N
// arms have no branch-merge machinery of their own the way
// `ifTrue:`/`ifFalse:`/`ifTrue:ifFalse:` do (BT-3489).
:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/storage_family_value_type_match_reject.bt
// => ERROR: Cannot assign to field 'self.total' inside a match: arm
